    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's not just about \"small acts\" though. it's the sheer volume of it. you see the same pain, the same preventable tragedies, over and over. it feels like I'm just standing in the middle of a massive flood with a tiny cup, trying to bail it out. eventually you realize the cup is useless. it feels like we're just delaying the inevitable and pretending there's some grand meaning to it when there isn't.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
